  "description": "NSF Senior Key Person Profile (Expanded) (NSF_KeyPersonExpanded_3_3) is an NSF-specific variant of the R&R Senior/Key Person Profile (Expanded) form.",
  "deviations": [
    "State/ZIP requirement: DAT shows asterisks on State and ZIP for some entries. The XSD marks both as optional. Resolution: follow the XSD. State is conditionally required when Country is USA.",
    "Degree Type and Degree Year: DAT includes Degree Type and Degree Year fields. The NSF XSD `PDPIProfileDataType` does NOT include `DegreeType` or `DegreeYear` elements (unlike the R&R Expanded form). These are managed via Research.gov and displayed read-only. Resolution: show these as read-only display fields, not submitted in XML.",
    "Attachment requirements: DAT indicates BioSketch, Current & Pending Support, and Collaborators are optional for Key Person, with only Synergistic Activities required. The XSD makes all 4 attachments required (not `minOccurs=\"0\"`) for BOTH PD/PI and Key Person. Resolution: follow the XSD. All 4 attachments are required for both.",
    "NSF ID for Key Person: The XSD `PersonProfileDataType` includes `NSFID` for Key Person, but DAT descriptions only reference NSF ID for the PD/PI. Resolution: follow the XSD. NSF ID is available for both.",
    "Department/Division maxLength: XSD uses V2 types (`DepartmentNameDataTypeV2`, `DivisionNameDataTypeV2`) with maxLength 100. We use the XSD constraint (100).",
    "ZIP/Postal Code maxLength: XSD defines `ZipPostalCodeDataType` with maxLength 30. We use the XSD constraint (30).",
    "Province maxLength: XSD defines `ProvinceDataType` with maxLength 30. We use the XSD constraint (30).",
    "Degree Type/Year not in XML: These fields are read-only display fields populated from Research.gov. They are NOT submitted in the XML and have no XML path.",
    "Organization UEI length: XSD defines `SAMUEIDataType` with exact `length 12` (not maxLength 13). We use the XSD constraint (exact length 12)."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "This is a low-volume NSF-specific form (2,082 submissions). Should be built after the generic R&R Expanded variant (FID 774).",
    "`PDPIProfileDataType` is similar but not identical to `PersonProfileDataType`: the PD/PI has NSF ID instead of Credential, and does not have DegreeType/DegreeYear. The Key Person section uses `PersonProfileDataType` which also has NSF ID and adds Organization UEI.",
    "All four attachment types are required for both PD/PI and Key Person per the XSD. This differs from DAT guidance and from the R&R Expanded base where only BioSketch is required.",
    "The NSF ProjectRole enum has only 3 values (PD/PI, Co-PD/PI, Other Senior Personnel), unlike the R&R Expanded form which has 13. This must be handled as a distinct enum, not reused from R&R.",
    "The NSF-specific fields (NSFID, Organization UEI) may require agency-specific validation that is not defined in the XSD."
  ],
